{"name":"Compaction Factor Test","type":"Fresh / Workability","destructive":False,"purpose":"Determines workability of fresh concrete, especially for mixes of low workability.","principle":"Ratio of partially compacted concrete mass to fully compacted concrete mass.","apparatus":["Compaction-factor apparatus","Trowel","Balance","Cylinder"],"procedure":["Fill the upper hopper without compaction.","Open the first gate and allow concrete to fall into the lower hopper.","Open the second gate and allow it into the cylinder.","Strike off and weigh partially compacted concrete.","Empty, refill and fully compact the cylinder; weigh it."],"result":"Report compaction factor as a dimensionless ratio.","formula":"CF = mass of partially compacted concrete / mass of fully compacted concrete","standard":"IS 1199","notes":"Lower values generally indicate lower workability."},
